ce in a business service organization and provides an opportunity to develop administrative, organizational, and customer service skills. Students will work alongside SBDC staff and have the opportunity to shadow Business Advisors and the Training Coordinator to gain exposure to small business assistance, training programs, client engagement, and community outreach activities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Greet clients and visitors in a professional and courteous manner. Answer phone calls and assist with general inquiries. Schedule, confirm, and manage appointments. Make copies, scan documents, and prepare materials for meetings, workshops, and events. File and organize records accurately and efficiently. Help prepare meeting rooms and training spaces for workshops, seminars, and events. Assist with client check-in and provide general customer service support. Ensure office areas remain clean, organized, and professional. Support staff with special projects assigned. Assist in maintaining the smooth and efficient day-to-day operations of the SBDC office. Security Sensitive: This position is classified as Security-Sensitive and is thereby subject to the provisions of Texas Education Code §51.215 and Texas Government Code §411.094, which authorize employers to obtain and review criminal history record information for applicants. Other Information An Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer It is the policy of Sul Ross State University to provide equal employment opportunity for all persons in accordance with their individual, job related qualifications and without consideration of race, creed, color, sex, religion, age, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status and ancestry. Equal employment opportunities shall be afforded in all personnel actions or decisions including, but not necessarily limited to, recruitment, hiring, training, upgrading, promotion, demotion, termination and salary. Retaliation is prohibited ag